    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1257">

                <pb facs="1244" n="1234" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg1234"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/2–1849: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cabot</hi>)<anchor n="49" xml:id="d1257-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-03-10T17:00:00-05:00">March 10, 1949—5
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>449. While Dept realizes practical problems to which ConGen doubtless refers
                    (Contel 462 Mar 3 to Emb rptd Dept 735 and Contel 399 Feb 18 to Emb rptd Dept
                        589<anchor n="50" xml:id="d1257-f2"/>) Dept believes desirable avoid
                    statements which might be open interpretation legal moral obligation
                    impartiality between sides China exists on part this Govt or its natls. US has
                    openly generously aided Natl Govt and has never recognized <pb facs="1245"
                        n="1235" xml:id="pg1235"/> belligerency Commie. This position in full accord
                    internatl law and practice.</p>
                <p>Dept had understood Chin Govt does not regard present strife China as “civil
                    war”. Emb comment requested whether Sun’s<anchor n="51" xml:id="d1257-f3"/>
                    reference civil war (third para Contel 742 Mar 4<anchor n="52" xml:id="d1257-f4"
                    /> press summary to Dept rptd unnumbered Emb) indicates change Chin Govt
                    position this question.</p>
                <p>If proposed contribution mentioned reftel not legally enforceable tax, ConGen
                    shld so advise Amer natls and shld advise further that they are obligated pay
                    only taxes officially imposed, as provided art 10 1946 treaty and that any case
                    duress shld be reported ConGen.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
